IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rta-speeding`

-- Road Traffic Act 1961 (Singapore) -- the figures behind speeding: which offences may be compounded and by whom (Road Traffic
-- (Composition of Offences) Rules, rule 2), and the Driver Improvement Points System (Road Traffic (Driver Improvement Points
-- System) Rules, rules 3, 3A, 4, 5 and 7 and the Schedule items (1) and (2) for exceeding a speed limit). Made under ss 135(2)
-- and 45(2) of the Act; the Act's side is in rta-speeding.l4.
--
-- Edition: Road Traffic (Composition of Offences) Rules (Cap. 276, R 29), informal consolidation in force from 6 September 2023,
-- as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/RTA1961-R29.txt; Road Traffic (Driver Improvement Points System) Rules
-- (Cap. 276, R 25), informal consolidation in force from 1 January 2026, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/RTA1961-R25.txt. Both retrieved from SSO on 13 October 2026.
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0273 (Haziq scenario, event from the Jun Hao scenario, event j084, 2049): a motorcyclist
-- caught at 25 km/h over the limit on an expressway -- the composition sum, the demerit points, and when the licence is suspended.
-- rta-speeding.l4 held these as labelled illustrative inputs; this module supplies the rules' figures beside it.
--
-- WHAT THE RULES DO NOT HOLD. R 29 says speeding under s 63(4) MAY be compounded and by whom; it fixes NO SUM. The sum is capped
-- by s 135(1) of the Act ($500 on a first offence, see rta-speeding.l4) and is otherwise a matter of an offer made by the
-- authorised officer (no scale is deposited). R 25 does not fix the new driver's REVOCATION threshold under s 35A: it borrows the
-- definition of "new driver" from the Road Traffic (New Drivers) Rules (R 32), not deposited. The expressway speed limit itself
-- (rules under s 63(1) or a notification under s 63(2)) is still an input.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: R 29 rule 2A (arrears before compounding certain checkpoint offences), rules 3 and 4 (payment, forms); R 25 rule
-- 3(3) (the register), rule 3A(2) (validity of a notice of eligibility), rule 4(6) (late-awarded points for an offence before a
-- clean year), rules 6, 8 and 9; the Schedule items other than (1) and (2), except as plain numbers in the cases; the precise
-- rolling of the 24- and 12-month windows "from the date of the first award" (rule 4(4)) -- points within the window are inputs.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Road Traffic Act 1961 -- composition rules and demerit points for speeding`

§§ `R 29 rule 2 -- speeding is compoundable`

-- R 29 rule 2: "The following offences may be compounded by the Deputy Commissioner of Police or any police officer not below the
-- rank of sergeant specially authorised by name in that behalf by the Deputy Commissioner of Police, or by any employee of the
-- Authority specially authorised by name in that behalf personally by the Registrar of Vehicles ..., in accordance with section
-- 135(1) of the Act: (a) the offences referred to in sections ... 63(4), ... of the Act; and (b) the offences under any rules or
-- orders made under the Act."
--
-- The rules name the offence and the officer. They name no sum: the only figure is the Act's ceiling in s 135(1).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `speeding is listed as compoundable in rule 2` IF TRUE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the composition rules fix a sum for speeding` IF FALSE

DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `the Deputy Commissioner of Police`
    `a sergeant or above specially authorised by name`
    `a police officer below the rank of sergeant`
    `a police officer not specially authorised`
    `an Authority employee specially authorised by name by the Registrar`
    `an Authority employee not specially authorised`

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may compound under rule 2` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `the Deputy Commissioner of Police` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a sergeant or above specially authorised by name` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a police officer below the rank of sergeant` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a police officer not specially authorised` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an Authority employee specially authorised by name by the Registrar` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an Authority employee not specially authorised` THEN FALSE

-- The sum an officer may offer: above nothing, and not above the s 135(1) cap (rta-speeding.l4). Whether the offer is $1 or $500
-- the deposited text does not say.
GIVEN `the sum offered` IS A NUMBER
      `has an earlier speeding conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the speeding composition offer is lawful` IF
        `speeding is listed as compoundable in rule 2`
    AND `may compound under rule 2` `the officer`
    AND `the composition sum is within the Act` `the sum offered` `has an earlier speeding conviction` TRUE

§§ `R 25 rule 3 and the Schedule -- demerit points for speeding`

-- R 25 rule 3(1): "Where a licence holder -- (a) is convicted of a scheduled offence; or (b) pays a sum of money to compound a
-- scheduled offence he is reasonably suspected to have committed, the Deputy Commissioner of Police shall award against that
-- holder the demerit points specified in the Schedule". Points follow composition as much as conviction, and "shall" leaves no
-- discretion.
GIVEN `convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `compounded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `demerit points must be awarded` IF `convicted` OR `compounded`

-- The Schedule, item (1) "Exceeding speed limit for vehicle" [Section 63(1) of the Act] and item (2) "Exceeding speed limit on a
-- road" [Section 63(4) of the Act], in the same bands:
--   (a) "by more than 0 but not more than 20 kilometres per hour"   6
--   (b) "by more than 20 but not more than 30 kilometres per hour"  8
--   (c) "by more than 30 but not more than 40 kilometres per hour"  12
--   (d) "by more than 40 but not more than 50 kilometres per hour"  18
--   (e) "by more than 50 kilometres per hour"                       24
-- A motorcycle's class limit (item 1) and an expressway's road limit (item 2) give the same points for the same excess.
GIVEN `the excess` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the demerit points for exceeding a speed limit` MEANS
    IF `the excess` AT MOST 0 THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the excess` AT MOST 20 THEN 6
        ELSE IF `the excess` AT MOST 30 THEN 8
            ELSE IF `the excess` AT MOST 40 THEN 12
                ELSE IF `the excess` AT MOST 50 THEN 18
                    ELSE 24

-- Rule 3(1A): for items (1)(a) to (e) and (2)(a) to (e), among others, committed "in a school zone, silver zone or zone demarcated
-- as "Friendly Streets"", the Deputy Commissioner "may award ... 2 demerit points in addition". (1B): in a zone demarcated as more
-- than one of those, "must not award ... more than 2 demerit points under paragraph (1A)". This gives the MOST that may be awarded.
GIVEN `the excess` IS A NUMBER
      `in a school zone` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in a silver zone` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in a Friendly Streets zone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most demerit points for speeding` MEANS
    IF `the excess` GREATER THAN 0 AND (`in a school zone` OR `in a silver zone` OR `in a Friendly Streets zone`)
    THEN `the demerit points for exceeding a speed limit` `the excess` + 2
    ELSE `the demerit points for exceeding a speed limit` `the excess`

§§ `R 25 rule 4 -- suspension`

-- Rule 4(1): "The Deputy Commissioner of Police may suspend, for a period not exceeding 36 months, the driving licence of any
-- person who has been awarded within a period of 24 months a total number of 24 or more demerit points."
-- (2): where the licence "has been suspended or is liable to suspension under paragraph (1), then notwithstanding paragraph (1),
-- whenever subsequently such person has been awarded within a period of 12 months a total number of 12 or more demerit points",
-- the Deputy Commissioner may suspend for not more than 36 months.
-- (3): (2) does not apply where the person "does not commit any scheduled offence for a period of 24 consecutive months
-- subsequent to the date his licence is liable to suspension or the date of expiry of the suspension or ... of the period for
-- which he is disqualified".
-- "may": reaching the threshold makes suspension AVAILABLE, not automatic (as s 45(3) of the Act).
-- INFERENCE: under the rule 4(2) regime the 24-in-24 test of (1) still applies too; "notwithstanding" adds a lower threshold.
GIVEN `previously suspended or liable to suspension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `24 clean months since` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rule 4(2) regime applies` IF
    `previously suspended or liable to suspension` AND (NOT `24 clean months since`)

GIVEN `points in 24 months` IS A NUMBER
      `points in 12 months` IS A NUMBER
      `under the rule 4(2) regime` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence is liable to suspension under rule 4` IF
        `points in 24 months` AT LEAST 24
    OR  (`under the rule 4(2) regime` AND `points in 12 months` AT LEAST 12)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rule 4 maximum suspension months` MEANS 36

-- How many more points before suspension becomes available, on the threshold that applies.
GIVEN `points so far` IS A NUMBER
      `under the rule 4(2) regime` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the further points before suspension` MEANS
    IF `under the rule 4(2) regime`
    THEN (IF `points so far` AT LEAST 12 THEN 0 ELSE 12 - `points so far`)
    ELSE (IF `points so far` AT LEAST 24 THEN 0 ELSE 24 - `points so far`)

-- Rule 4(5): where the holder "does not commit any scheduled offence for any period of 12 consecutive months, excluding any period
-- for which his driving licence is suspended ... or ... he is disqualified ..., every demerit point awarded against him before that
-- period shall be disregarded". (Rule 4(6), the late award for an offence before the clean year, is NOT ENCODED.)
GIVEN `points before the clean year` IS A NUMBER
      `points after it` IS A NUMBER
      `a clean 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the points that count` MEANS
    IF `a clean 12 months` THEN `points after it` ELSE `points before the clean year` + `points after it`

-- Rule 5(1): the Deputy Commissioner "shall notify the holder ... of the date on which he intends to suspend his driving licence
-- and shall require him to show cause within 14 days from the date of the notice". The Act's s 46(1) separately requires the
-- suspension date to be at least 4 weeks after the notice (rta-speeding.l4). Days are counted from an arbitrary origin.
GIVEN `the day of the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day to show cause` MEANS `the day of the notice` + 14

§§ `R 25 rule 3A -- the safe-driving course`

-- Rule 3A(1): the Deputy Commissioner "must issue a notice of eligibility" if (a) among other criteria, the holder is not "a new
-- driver in relation to any class of driving licence", the licence is not suspended or liable to suspension under rule 4, the
-- holder is not disqualified, and demerit points have been disregarded under (3) on not more than one previous occasion in 10
-- years and not in the last 12 months; and (b) a scheduled offence's points bring the holder to "(i) in any case where the licence
-- holder is a person referred to in rule 4(2) ..., a total of 4 or more demerit points within a period of 12 months; or ...
-- (iii) in any other case, a total of 8 or more demerit points within a period of 24 months."
-- The criteria in (a) other than those named are taken as a single input. (Foreign-licence criteria are NOT ENCODED.)
GIVEN `points in 24 months` IS A NUMBER
      `points in 12 months` IS A NUMBER
      `under the rule 4(2) regime` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the course trigger is reached` IF
    IF `under the rule 4(2) regime`
    THEN `points in 12 months` AT LEAST 4
    ELSE `points in 24 months` AT LEAST 8

GIVEN `points in 24 months` IS A NUMBER
      `points in 12 months` IS A NUMBER
      `under the rule 4(2) regime` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a new driver on any class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `disregards in the last 10 years` IS A NUMBER
      `a disregard in the last 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other criteria are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a notice of eligibility must issue` IF
        (NOT `a new driver on any class`)
    AND (NOT `the licence is liable to suspension under rule 4` `points in 24 months` `points in 12 months` `under the rule 4(2) regime`)
    AND `disregards in the last 10 years` AT MOST 1
    AND (NOT `a disregard in the last 12 months`)
    AND `the other criteria are met`
    AND `the course trigger is reached` `points in 24 months` `points in 12 months` `under the rule 4(2) regime`

-- Rule 3A(3): from the date the holder "successfully completes a Course ..., the Deputy Commissioner of Police may disregard 4 of the
-- demerit points that would otherwise be taken into account". This gives the count if the 4 are disregarded.
GIVEN `points counted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the points counted after the course` MEANS
    IF `points counted` AT LEAST 4 THEN `points counted` - 4 ELSE 0

§§ `R 25 rule 7 -- foreign driving licences`

-- Rule 7(1): the Deputy Commissioner may "(a) prohibit the holder of a foreign driving licence who has been awarded a total of 13
-- or more demerit points within a period of 12 months from the date of the grant of that licence from driving ... for a period of
-- 12 months; or (b) prohibit the holder ... who has been awarded a total of 24 or more demerit points within a period of 24
-- consecutive months ... for a period not exceeding 36 months."
GIVEN `points in the first 12 months of the foreign licence` IS A NUMBER
      `points in 24 months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a prohibition order is available` IF
        `points in the first 12 months of the foreign licence` AT LEAST 13
    OR  `points in 24 months` AT LEAST 24

§§ `The REQ-0273 question with the rules' figures`

DECLARE RiderRecord HAS
    `the limit in force` IS A NUMBER
    `the speed recorded` IS A NUMBER
    `points already in 24 months` IS A NUMBER
    `points already in 12 months` IS A NUMBER
    `earlier suspended or liable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `clean for 24 months since` IS A BOOLEAN
    `earlier speeding conviction` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the rider` IS A RiderRecord
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rider's excess` MEANS `the excess over the limit` (`the rider`'s `the limit in force`) (`the rider`'s `the speed recorded`)

GIVEN `the rider` IS A RiderRecord
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rider's new points` MEANS `the demerit points for exceeding a speed limit` (`the rider's excess` `the rider`)

GIVEN `the rider` IS A RiderRecord
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rider is under rule 4(2)` IF
    `the rule 4(2) regime applies` (`the rider`'s `earlier suspended or liable`) (`the rider`'s `clean for 24 months since`)

GIVEN `the rider` IS A RiderRecord
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rider's points in 24 months` MEANS `the rider`'s `points already in 24 months` + `the rider's new points` `the rider`

GIVEN `the rider` IS A RiderRecord
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rider's points in 12 months` MEANS `the rider`'s `points already in 12 months` + `the rider's new points` `the rider`

GIVEN `the rider` IS A RiderRecord
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rider's licence may be suspended` IF
    `the licence is liable to suspension under rule 4` (`the rider's points in 24 months` `the rider`) (`the rider's points in 12 months` `the rider`) (`the rider is under rule 4(2)` `the rider`)

GIVEN `the rider` IS A RiderRecord
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rider's further points before suspension` MEANS
    IF `the rider is under rule 4(2)` `the rider`
    THEN `the further points before suspension` (`the rider's points in 12 months` `the rider`) TRUE
    ELSE `the further points before suspension` (`the rider's points in 24 months` `the rider`) FALSE

GIVEN `the rider` IS A RiderRecord
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rider's composition cap` MEANS `the composition cap for speeding` (`the rider`'s `earlier speeding conviction`)
